# SetBodyPose
#
# Persistent set-and-hold for Go2 sport API Euler(1007) +
# BalanceStand(1002). The bridge continuously republishes the target
# rpy at 50Hz to fight the balance controller (v1-v6 演进见
# body_pose_bridge_node.hpp 文件头)。
#
# 2026-10-13 简化:body_h 字段去除。Go2 固件(2026-10-10 真机验证)对
# BodyHeight api(1013)bh_off 参数不响应,act body_h 在 bh_off=0 vs
# bh_off=-0.18 几乎无差别(差 ≤ 2mm),参见 feedback memory
# feedback_go2_bodyheight_1013_unresponsive。SetBodyPose 因此退化为
# 仅控 rpy;lower/raise body 的需求由 StandUp(身高档位)覆盖。
#
# See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-body-pose-bridge-design.md §4.1.

# ---- Request ----
# Standard right-hand-rule Euler angles (rad).
# NOTE: Go2 firmware inverts the pitch convention — pitch>0 = nose DOWN
# (verified on real hardware 2026-10-10). Caller must use the inverted
# sign for "nose down forward-tilt".
float64 roll
float64 pitch
float64 yaw
# If true, bridge cancels its 50Hz republish and sends a final
# Euler(0,0,0) + BalanceStand sequence. rpy fields are IGNORED in this
# case. Used to release the bridge so StandDown / Move can take over the
# /api/sport/request channel.
bool clear
---
# ---- Response ----
bool success
string message
